===Etymology===
From Arabic {{Arab|[[محمد]]}} (''muħámmad'', [[praise]]d, [[commendable]], [[laudable]]), the past participle of {{Arab|[[حمد]]}} (''ħámida'', to [[praise]], [[commend]], [[laud]], [[extol]]).

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# The [[prophet]] who [[introduce]]d [[Islam]], the man to whom the [[Quran]] was [[reveal]]ed.
# {{given name|male|from=Arabic}} very popular among [[Muslim]]s.

====Derived terms====
* [[Mohammedan]] ([[Mohammedanism]]), [[Mohammedism]] {{qualifier|now offensive}}
* [[Mohammedist]] {{qualifier|rare, offensive}}

